==English==

{{Webster 1913}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|extortus|lang=la}}, past participle of {{term|extorquere||to [[twist]] or [[wrench]] out, to extort|lang=la}}; from {{term|ex||out|lang=la}} + {{term|-tort}}, from {{term/t|la|torqueō||twist, turn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɔː(r)t}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[wrest]] from an [[unwilling]] person by physical force, menace, duress, torture, or any undue or illegal exercise of power or ingenuity; to wrench away (from); to [[tear]] away; to [[wring]] (from); to [[exact]]; as, to extort contributions from the vanquished; to extort confessions of guilt; to extort a promise; to extort payment of a debt.
# {{context|transitive|legal|lang=en}} To obtain by means of the offense of [[extortion]].
# {{context|transitive|and|intransitive|medicine|ophthalmology|lang=en}} To twist outwards.

